00:00:01,171 --> 00:00:11,119
In the Seebeck effect, a temperature difference between two junctions of different metals makes an e m f, set by the metals and the temperature difference.

3
00:00:11,119 --> 00:00:16,966
The thermoelectric series gives the direction: earlier to later through the cold junction.

4
00:00:16,966 --> 00:00:25,911
In the Peltier effect, a current heats one junction and cools the other, H equals pi I t, reversible, unlike Joule heating.

5
00:00:25,911 --> 00:00:36,158
The e m f follows a parabola, with the neutral temperature at minus alpha over beta and inversion at two theta n minus theta c.

6
00:00:36,158 --> 00:00:41,015
And a thermopile adds many couples in series to detect radiation.

